  em,enchantress,page_text,11082,"Best Enchantress Commanders for EDH | EDHMatch\nEDHMatchFind commanders that match how you play\nHome\nFind CommandersCommander QuizCommander DNAWhat Should I Build Next?Advanced SearchCollectionsColor Combinations\nTwo-Color Guilds\nAzorius\nDimir\nRakdos\nGruul\nSelesnya\nOrzhov\nIzzet\nGolgari\nBoros\nSimic\nThree-Color Combinations\nJund\nEsper\nGrixis\nBant\nNaya\nAbzan\nJeskai\nSultai\nMardu\nTemur\nMono-Color\nMono-White\nMono-Blue\nMono-Black\nMono-Red\nMono-Green\nColorless\nColorless\nBrowse by SetBrowse All\nDiscover PlaystylePlayer Type QuizGuild Quiz\nStrategies\nShortlist\nBlog\nNewsletter\nSearch\nSearch\nHome\nFind Commanders\nCommander Quiz\nCommander DNA\nWhat Should I Build Next?\nAdvanced Search\nCollections\nColor CombinationsTwo-Color Guilds\nAzorius\nDimir\nRakdos\nGruul\nSelesnya\nOrzhov\nIzzet\nGolgari\nBoros\nSimic\nThree-Color Combinations\nJund\nEsper\nGrixis\nBant\nNaya\nAbzan\nJeskai\nSultai\nMardu\nTemur\nMono-Color\nMono-White\nMono-Blue\nMono-Black\nMono-Red\nMono-Green\nColorless\nColorless\nBrowse by Set\nBrowse All\nDiscover Playstyle\nPlayer Type Quiz\nGuild Quiz\nStrategies\nShortlist\nBlog\nNewsletter\nEDHMatchThe data platform for Commander. Find commanders that fit how you actually play.\nExplore\nHome\nSearch\nQuiz\nWhat Should I Build Next?\nBlog\nDiscover\nCollections\nSets\nBudget\nStrategy Guides\nAll Themes\nTokens\nSacrifice\nLifegain\nCompany\nNewsletter\nAbout\nContact\nLegal\nAffiliate Disclosure\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms & Conditions\nCookie Settings\nMagic: The Gathering and its logos are trademarks of Wizards of the Coast LLC. This site is not affiliated with Wizards of the Coast LLC.© 2026 EDHMATCH\nEDHMatchFind commanders that match how you play\nHome\nFind CommandersCommander QuizCommander DNAWhat Should I Build Next?Advanced SearchCollectionsColor Combinations\nTwo-Color Guilds\nAzorius\nDimir\nRakdos\nGruul\nSelesnya\nOrzhov\nIzzet\nGolgari\nBoros\nSimic\nThree-Color Combinations\nJund\nEsper\nGrixis\nBant\nNaya\nAbzan\nJeskai\nSultai\nMardu\nTemur\nMono-Color\nMono-White\nMono-Blue\nMono-Black\nMono-Red\nMono-Green\nColorless\nColorless\nBrowse by SetBrowse All\nDiscover PlaystylePlayer Type QuizGuild Quiz\nStrategies\nShortlist\nBlog\nNewsletter\nSearch\nSearch\nHome\nFind Commanders\nCommander Quiz\nCommander DNA\nWhat Should I Build Next?\nAdvanced Search\nCollections\nColor CombinationsTwo-Color Guilds\nAzorius\nDimir\nRakdos\nGruul\nSelesnya\nOrzhov\nIzzet\nGolgari\nBoros\nSimic\nThree-Color Combinations\nJund\nEsper\nGrixis\nBant\nNaya\nAbzan\nJeskai\nSultai\nMardu\nTemur\nMono-Color\nMono-White\nMono-Blue\nMono-Black\nMono-Red\nMono-Green\nColorless\nColorless\nBrowse by Set\nBrowse All\nDiscover Playstyle\nPlayer Type Quiz\nGuild Quiz\nStrategies\nShortlist\nBlog\nNewsletter\nHome\nStrategies\nEnchantress\nBack to SearchBest Enchantress Commanders for EDH\nEnchantress decks are for players who want each enchantment cast to replace itself and add another layer to the board. This strategy wants to chain cheap enchantments, using enchantress commanders, draw engines, and protective pieces, to win through constellation triggers, token makers, or an aura-based Voltron line. Unlike general Card Draw decks, Enchantress ties its cards to enchantment casts, and unlike Lifegain it treats life from Sythis-style triggers as support rather than the main engine. The best enchantment decks EDH players build feel incremental: ramp a little, draw a card, protect the engine, then convert the chain into threats.\nBest Colors for Enchantress Decks\nSelesnya supplies classic enchantress draw, aura ramp, protection, and enchantment removal.\nBant adds blue counterspells, extra draw, and aura tools to protect the enchantment engine.\nOrzhov trades green draw creatures for removal enchantments, drain, and Daxos-style token payoffs.\nHow Do Enchantress Decks Win in Commander?\nEnchantress decks excel through a specific playstyle and win conditions. Here's how they work:\n✓ You cast cheap enchantments that replace themselves through enchantress triggers.\n✓ You stack two or more draw engines so each spell keeps the chain moving.\n✓ You protect the engine with shroud effects recursion and enchantment-based removal.\n✓ You convert repeated casts into tokens counters life or larger attackers.\n✓ You finish with constellation payoffs an aura Voltron threat or a sustained card lead.\nBest Cards for Enchantress EDH Decks\nArgothian Enchantress\nCheap protected draw engine that rewards every enchantment you cast.\nEnchantress's Presence\nEnchantress draw on an enchantment, making the engine harder to remove.\nSythis, Harvest's Hand\nPuts card draw and lifegain in the command zone for each enchantment cast.\nSterling Grove\nProtects your enchantments and tutors the missing engine piece when needed.\nSigil of the Empty Throne\nConverts later enchantment casts into Angel tokens that close through combat.\nHow to Build a Enchantress Commander Deck\nCore Components\n✓Run 6-10 enchantress effects such as Argothian Enchantress, Enchantress's Presence, Setessan Champion, and Mesa Enchantress\n✓Fill the curve with cheap enchantments like Wild Growth, Utopia Sprawl, and removal auras\n✓Include protection such as Sterling Grove, Greater Auramancy, and Heroic Intervention\n✓Add recursion like Hall of Heliod's Generosity to rebuild after sweepers\nDeck Structure\n✓Keep the average mana value low so one- and two-mana enchantments trigger more draws\n✓Use enchantment ramp like Sanctum Weaver, Wild Growth, and Fertile Ground as acceleration and triggers\n✓Play 34-36 lands because aura ramp and steady draw smooth land drops\n✓Favor enchantment removal like Grasp of Fate and Darksteel Mutation over spells that do not trigger engines\nWin Conditions\n✓Use Sigil of the Empty Throne or Ajani's Chosen to turn casts into tokens\n✓Grow Setessan Champion or constellation payoffs as a natural result of playing enchantments\n✓Stack auras on one protected creature when an aura Voltron line is open\n✓Win longer games by drawing more cards than opponents can trade for\nWeaknesses of Enchantress Decks\n⚠Killing early enchantress creatures can leave you casting enchantments without drawing cards.\n⚠Mass enchantment removal like Farewell or Bane of Progress can undo several turns of setup.\n⚠The engine often needs time to assemble, which leaves openings for fast combo or combat decks.\n⚠Hands full of payoffs but few cheap enchantments can stall before the chain starts.\nIs Enchantress Right for You?\nEnchantress is a friendly engine deck because the core loop is simple: cast an enchantment, draw a card, keep going. It suits players who enjoy building a protected board over several turns rather than racing combat early. Sythis keeps budget builds functional, while premium pieces mostly add speed and resilience.\nRelated Commander Strategies\nCard Draw\nCard Draw is broader; Enchantress draws specifically from casting enchantments.\nVoltron\nVoltron can use Auras; Enchantress treats aura attacks as one payoff line.\nLifegain\nLifegain makes life the engine; Enchantress uses life as support for enchantment chains.\nBrowse Commander Lists\nTop Enchantress CommandersAurasLifegain\nTop Enchantress Commanders\nMarina Vendrell\nMV: 5\nEnchantressRoomsCombo+7 more\n$0.28TCGPlayer\n€0.13CardMarket\nGo-Shintai of Life's Origin\nMV: 4\nEnchantressShrinesTokens+7 more\n$8.36TCGPlayer\n€10.75CardMarket\nAnikthea, Hand of Erebos\nMV: 5\nEnchantressReanimatorTokens+7 more\nN/ATCGPlayer\nN/ACardMarket\nSythis, Harvest's Hand\nMV: 2\nEnchantressAurasLifegain+7 more\n$4.32TCGPlayer\n€2.83CardMarket\nAminatou, Veil Piercer\nMV: 4\nEnchantressTopdeckControl+7 more\n$0.64TCGPlayer\n€0.75CardMarket\nBello, Bard of the Brambles\nMV: 3\nEnchantressArtifactsUnnatural+7 more\n$2.87TCGPlayer\n€3.35CardMarket\nTuvasa the Sunlit\nMV: 3\nEnchantressAurasVoltron+7 more\nN/ATCGPlayer\nN/ACardMarket\nThe Master of Keys\nMV: 3\nEnchantressReanimatorMill+7 more\n$2.82TCGPlayer\n€0.95CardMarket\nZur, Eternal Schemer\nMV: 3\nEnchantressLifegainControl+7 more\n$4.32TCGPlayer\n€4.21CardMarket\nTerra, Magical Adept // Esper Terra\nMV: 3Universes Beyond\nEnchantressSagasCombo+7 more\n$2.25TCGPlayer\n€2.32CardMarket\nTom Bombadil\nMV: 5Universes Beyond\nSagasEnchantressHistoric+7 more\n$3.58TCGPlayer\n€3.04CardMarket\nZur the Enchanter\nMV: 4\nEnchantressAurasStax+7 more\n$1.55TCGPlayer\n€0.71CardMarket\nEriette of the Charmed Apple\nMV: 3\nAurasEnchantressLifegain+7 more\n$1.20TCGPlayer\n€1.73CardMarket\nAlela, Artful Provocateur\nMV: 4\nEnchantressFaeriesArtifacts+7 more\n$1.36TCGPlayer\n€0.51CardMarket\nTatsunari, Toad Rider\nMV: 3\nEnchantressAurasMutate+7 more\n$0.30TCGPlayer\n€0.13CardMarket\nKillian, Decisive Mentor\nMV: 3\nAurasEnchantressForced Combat+7 more\n$0.83TCGPlayer\n€0.82CardMarket\nWildsear, Scouring Maw\nMV: 5\nEnchantressCascadeAuras+7 more\nN/ATCGPlayer\nN/ACardMarket\nNarci, Fable Singer\nMV: 4\nSagasEnchantressLifegain+7 more\nN/ATCGPlayer\nN/ACardMarket\nEllivere of the Wild Court\nMV: 4\nAurasEnchantressHatebears+7 more\n$0.42TCGPlayer\n€0.48CardMarket\nLight-Paws, Emperor's Voice\nMV: 2\nAurasVoltronEnchantress+7 more\n$1.66TCGPlayer\n€4.99CardMarket\nVictor, Valgavoth's Seneschal\nMV: 3\nEnchantressReanimatorAuras+7 more\n$0.32TCGPlayer\n€0.18CardMarket\nEstrid, the Masked\nMV: 4\nEnchantressAurasPlaneswalkers+7 more\nN/ATCGPlayer\nN/ACardMarket\nMyrkul, Lord of Bones\nMV: 7\nEnchantressTokensAristocrats+7 more\n$0.25TCGPlayer\n€0.17CardMarket\nYenna, Redtooth Regent\nMV: 4\nAurasEnchantressTokens+7 more\n$2.17TCGPlayer\n€1.70CardMarket\nLynde, Cheerful Tormentor\nMV: 4\nCursesEnchantressAuras+7 more\n$1.28TCGPlayer\n€0.84CardMarket\nFilter and browse all Enchantress commanders →\nFrequently Asked Questions\nWhat makes a good Enchantress commander?\nThe best enchantress commanders typically provide consistent access to the strategy's core mechanics. Look for commanders that you cast cheap enchantments that replace themselves through enchantress triggers.\nHow do Enchantress decks win?\nEnchantress decks win through a combination of Argothian Enchantress, Enchantress's Presence, Sythis, Harvest's Hand, and other synergistic pieces that enchantress decks are for players who want each enchantment cast to replace itself and add another layer to the board.\nWhat are the best colors for Enchantress?\nSelesnya supplies classic enchantress draw, aura ramp, protection, and enchantment removal. However, Bant adds blue counterspells, extra draw, and aura tools to protect the enchantment engine.\nWhat are the weaknesses of Enchantress decks?\nKilling early enchantress creatures can leave you casting enchantments without drawing cards. Mass enchantment removal like Farewell or Bane of Progress can undo several turns of setup. The engine often needs time to assemble, which leaves openings for fast combo or combat decks. Hands full of payoffs but few cheap enchantments can stall before the chain starts.\nEDHMatchThe data platform for Commander. Find commanders that fit how you actually play.\nExplore\nHome\nSearch\nQuiz\nWhat Should I Build Next?\nBlog\nDiscover\nCollections\nSets\nBudget\nStrategy Guides\nAll Themes\nTokens\nSacrifice\nLifegain\nCompany\nNewsletter\nAbout\nContact\nLegal\nAffiliate Disclosure\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms & Conditions\nCookie Settings\nMagic: The Gathering and its logos are trademarks of Wizards of the Coast LLC. This site is not affiliated with Wizards of the Coast LLC.© 2026 EDHMATCH"
